 "notes": "Output-only task. The two accepted C++ (5671315, 5671318) branch on the test number into plans tuned to official files 4-10 and on any other input index arr[n - 30] in a debug loop, so they segfault on valid inputs with fewer than 30 shrimp (most generated inputs; on nemo10.in they also print their plan twice); they are no reference and their files are gone. orig.cpp: greedy chases by earliest interception (least root of |s(t) - pos| = V (t - now)) or by weight per unit of chase time, keeping the heavier plan; it matches the sample, is valid on the ten official files and 150 generated inputs, and equals an exhaustive search over eating orders on 79 of 81 inputs with at most 7 shrimp. checker.py replays the plan to 1e-4 and accepts any valid plan that eats at least as much. Bounds come from the official nemo1-10.in (n <= 10000, T <= 10000, V <= 1000), since the statement gives none."
